---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Docs"
  description="Driftstack documentation: quickstart, SDK references for TypeScript / Python / Go, API reference, self-hosted setup, recipe library."
>
  <!-- Header -->
  <section class="bg-gradient-to-b from-white to-slate-50">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-20">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-oxblood-700">Docs</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-slate-900 md:text-5xl">
        Everything you need to drive a session.
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-prose text-lg text-slate-600">
        Quickstarts for every supported language, the full API reference,
        SDK guides, self-hosted setup, and the recipe catalogue. Driftstack
        is small enough to read end-to-end — start with the quickstart
        and follow the link trail.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Doc categories -->
  <section class="border-t border-slate-200 bg-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-16">
      <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
        <a
          href="/docs/quickstart"
          class="group rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm transition hover:border-oxblood-700"
        >
          <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-oxblood-700">
            Quickstart
          </p>
          <h2 class="mt-3 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900 group-hover:text-oxblood-700">
            Five minutes to first session →
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-600">
            Install the SDK in your language, paste an API key, drive
            your first session. No prior browser-automation experience
            needed.
          </p>
        </a>

        <a
          href="/api-reference"
          class="group rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm transition hover:border-oxblood-700"
        >
          <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-oxblood-700">
            API reference
          </p>
          <h2 class="mt-3 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900 group-hover:text-oxblood-700">
            Every endpoint, every shape →
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-600">
            Auto-generated from the OpenAPI 3.1 spec. Try requests
            against your own API key directly in the browser. Same
            spec the SDK codegen reads.
          </p>
        </a>

        <a
          href="/docs/sdk"
          class="group rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm transition hover:border-oxblood-700"
        >
          <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-oxblood-700">SDKs</p>
          <h2 class="mt-3 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900 group-hover:text-oxblood-700">
            TypeScript · Python · Go →
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-600">
            Native packages on npm, PyPI, and as a Go module. Typed
            request/response shapes. Retry-with-backoff. Webhook
            signature verification. Async iterators for paginated
            list endpoints.
          </p>
        </a>

        <a
          href="/docs/webhooks"
          class="group rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm transition hover:border-oxblood-700"
        >
          <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-oxblood-700">Webhooks</p>
          <h2 class="mt-3 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900 group-hover:text-oxblood-700">
            Event types + signature verification →
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-600">
            All five event types — session.completed, session.failed,
            api_key.revoked, quota.warning_80pct, quota.exceeded — with
            payload shapes and HMAC-SHA256 verification examples.
          </p>
        </a>

        <a
          href="/self-hosted"
          class="group rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm transition hover:border-oxblood-700"
        >
          <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-oxblood-700">
            Self-hosted
          </p>
          <h2 class="mt-3 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900 group-hover:text-oxblood-700">
            Deploy on your own hardware →
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-600">
            SKU comparison, hardware specs, onboarding flow. For
            sustained high-concurrency operations or full data
            sovereignty.
          </p>
        </a>

        <a
          href="/docs/recipes"
          class="group rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm transition hover:border-oxblood-700"
        >
          <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-oxblood-700">
            Recipe library
          </p>
          <h2 class="mt-3 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900 group-hover:text-oxblood-700">
            Pre-built session scripts →
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-600">
            Phase 3 — login forms, SMS-OTP flows, multi-step checkouts.
            Recipe interface lands today (mock implementation), real
            catalogue ships once Phase 3 closes.
          </p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Help banner -->
  <section class="border-t border-slate-200 bg-slate-50">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-12">
      <div class="flex flex-col items-start gap-4 md:flex-row md:items-center md:justify-between">
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900">Doc not landing?</h2>
          <p class="mt-2 max-w-prose text-sm text-slate-600">
            Email <a
              href="mailto:support@driftstack.dev"
              class="text-oxblood-700 underline">support@driftstack.dev</a> with the URL you expected to find. We answer in writing,
            usually same business day.
          </p>
        </div>
        <a href="https://github.com/driftstackdev" class="btn-secondary">GitHub →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
